TECH_MV IOPAD V125 PAYLOAD MANIFEST
====================================
Formal runtime targets:
  build_PR/run/tool/TT_tool_iopad_innovus_local_bridge.tcl
  build_PR/run/tool/TT_flow_iopad_interface_start.tcl
  build_PR/run/tool/ioPADt/*

V125 key policy:
  - IO_FILE is optional; no-IO discovery can use generated Tcl or live bridge.
  - Discovery side families: FILL_IN_CELL_DIGITAL_IO_PAD_050, FILL_IN_CELL_RTE_BOUNDARY_PAD_051, FILL_IN_CELL_CORE_POWER_PAD_042, FILL_IN_CELL_IO_POWER_PAD_043, FILL_IN_CELL_IO_RAIL_CUT_052.
  - Confirmed corner master: FILL_IN_CELL_IO_CORNER_053.
  - Runtime snapshots/bootstrap files live under ioPADt/build/.
  - Minimum PAD spacing is 15.0 units and offset spacing/anchor checks block Save/Apply.
  - ESD maps to ESD; VSS maps to VSS; the two rails are independent.
  - Reset ALL Global Net clears working state without touching the source Tcl.
  - Newly introduced nets get create_net -physical -ground -name <NET> plus skip_routing.
  - read_io_file always uses -no_die_size_adjust.
  - Backups are stored under PROJECT_ROOT/backup/.

SHA256 checksums are provided by the installer package SHA256SUMS file.
